# Wave W17-X (Route 212 — South): bog turf — bog-edge turf, reed flecks: an olive bog green carrying straw reed flecks and dark bog flecks, the dry edge of the wet country where the shipped marshbog biome stands byte-preserved in this ground’s field (design: the road admitting defeat into deepening bog pools; Fenland’s roofs show over the reeds). Route 212 — South’s own ground — split from Route 212 — North’s wet meadow by the olive entire: the North is learning, the South is the bog itself.
